  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 — MIME string validation (additive, fully backwards-compatible)\n\nAdded:\n- MimeValidator.IsKnownMimeType(string) and GetKnownMimeTypes() — validate user-supplied MIME-type strings against canonical types, their aliases, and signature-less types. Case- and whitespace-insensitive.\n- MimeSignature.Aliases (optional string[]) — alternate MIME names co-located with byte signatures (e.g. text/xml, image/jpg, application/x-zip-compressed, audio/mp3). Recognized by IsKnownMimeType but never returned by the detector.\n- SignatureDatabase.GetAllMimeTypesIncludingAliases().\n- MimeTypes constants: TextXml, Csv, Markdown, Yaml, XHtml, JsonLd, FormUrlEncoded, MultipartFormData.\n\nUnchanged:\n- MimeDetector.Detect continues to return canonical MIME types only.\n- MimeValidator.GetSupportedMimeTypes() continues to return only bytes-detectable types.\n- All existing constants, validation pipelines, AspNetCore middleware, attributes, and services are byte-for-byte compatible with 1.x.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/vijaypratap12/MimeCheck/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
